L283: TRIAL SUMMARY
L284: | Trial Title | Early administration of Vitamin C in patients with sepsis or septic shock in emergency departments: a multicentre, double blinded, randomized controlled trial: the C-EASIE trial. |
L285: | --- | --- |
L286: | Short title | C-EASIE trial: Vitamin C - Early Administration in Sepsis In ED |
L287: | Internal reference | S63213 |
L288: | Trial Design | Randomized, Double Blinded, Multicentre Controlled Trial |
L289: | Trial Participants and setting | Patients presenting with sepsis or septic shock in the Emergency Department |
L290: | Intervention(s) | Ascorbic Acid 1.5g IV in 50ml Normal Saline every 6hrs, started within 6hrs after presentation at the emergency department |
L291: | Control | Placebo (Normal Saline 50ml every 6hrs) |
L292: | Primary Endpoint | Average post-baseline patient SOFA score (on day 2-5 after patient inclusion). |
L293: | Secondary Endpoint(s) | 28-day mortality Maximum SOFA score Length of hospital stay Length of ICU stay Vasopressor requirement: total duration and dosage RRT duration and need Ventilator days Total dose of steroids given Quality of life (EQ-5D-5L) Time to return to work (if applicable) Lab values :  Creatinine, CRP and Sodium on d1-5 Procalcitonin on d1 and d4 |
L294: | Planned Sample Size | 300 |
L295: | Treatment duration | 4 days (a total of 16 doses) |
L296: | Follow up duration | 3 months |
L297: | Duration of the trial (FPI-CSR) | Recruitment period: 18 months Maximum duration of the trial: 27 months |
L298: ROLE OF STUDY SPONSOR AND FUNDER
L299: University Hospitals Leuven as mentioned in KEY TRIAL CONTACT shall act as sponsor of the Study, as defined in the Law of 2004, and shall assume all responsibilities and liabilities in connection therewith and procure the mandatory liability insurance coverage in accordance with the Law of 2004. University Hospitals Leuven shall ensure that it shall be mentioned in the Protocol, the Informed Consent Forms and in other relevant communication with the Study Subjects or the Regulatory Authorities as sponsor of the Study. University Hospitals Leuven acknowledges and agrees for the avoidance of doubt that KCE shall under no circumstances be considered as sponsor of the Study or assume any responsibilities or liabilities in connection therewith, and University Hospitals Leuven shall make no representations whatsoever in this respect.
L300: ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF TRIAL MANAGEMENT COMMITEES
L301: Trial Steering Committee (TSC)
L302: The role of the Trial Steering Committee (TSC) is to provide the overall supervision of the trial. The TSC will also include members who are independent of the investigators, their employing organisations, funders and sponsors. The TSC should monitor trial progress, conduct and advise on scientific credibility. The TSC will consider and act, as appropriate, and ultimately carries the responsibility for deciding whether a trial needs to be stopped on grounds of safety or efficacy.
L303: The TSC will meet on average 3 times per year the first year and twice the year after that. The TSC is composed of the CI, the trial statistician, the trial PM, an independent expert, a representative of other participating centres or groups, 2 patients or members of the public, 1 representative of the sponsor and 1 representative of the funder.
L304: The day-to-day management of the study will be performed by the Trial Management Group (TMG) which is distinct from the TSC.
L305: Members TSC
L306: CI: Dr. Didier Desruelles
L307: Co-CI: Dr. Stefanie Vandervelden
L308: Trial statistician: Steffen Fieuws
L309: Project manager/Trial Coordinator: Lina Wauters
L310: Independent expert: Prof. Maaret Castren
L311: Representatives participating centers: Dr Jan Breuls (AZ Turnhout), Dr Philippe Meersseman (UZ Leuven), Dr Ken Dewitte (UZA), Dr Philippe Vanhove (GZA), Dr. Evert Verhoeven (UZ Brussel), Dr. Francois Stifkens (CHU Liège), Dr Magali Bartiaux (CHU St Pierre Bruxelles), Dr. Jacques Creteur (ULB Hôpital Erasme)
L312: Representative CTC: Ine Vanopdenbosch
L313: Representative of the funder
L314: Member of the public (patient): Mr Dave Carson
L315: Data Monitoring Committee (DMC)
L316: The role of the Data Monitoring Committee (DMC) is to safeguard the interests of study participants, assess the safety and efficacy of study procedures, and monitor the overall conduct of the study.
L317: The DMC will include at least four members: the chair, an executive secretary, independent statistician and minimum one expert independent of the investigators.
L318: The DMC will meet after 50 patients have completed treatment and will review the study data and advise on the continuation of the trial. They will monitor all participating sites until all patients are recruited.  The DMC will then meet annually to discuss the progress of the trial.
L319: The DMC will report to the TSC according to the DMC charter.
