L552: ## Trial assessments
L553: Baseline:
L554: NEWS score will be calculated at ED presentation (1st set of vital signs measured).
L555: The EQ-5D-5L health questionnaire will be obtained. If the patient’s clinical status doesn’t allow self-completion, the questionnaire may be completed by proxy.
L556: A pregnancy test will be performed for women of child bearing potential. If not included in the standard of care (BetaHCG on blood sample), a urine test will be performed on study budget.
L557: *Initially the patient will be asked if she reached menopause. If the answer is no, a pregnancy test will be performed. When in doubt or when it is impossible to ask the patient, a pregnancy test will be performed in every female patient ≤ 55 years old.
L558: By visit:
L559: Daily assessments (day 1-5):
L560: - Administration of study drug.
L561: - Calculation of SOFA score.
L562: - Vital signs (GCS, HR, BP, SpO2).
L563: - Clinical data collection for assessment of study outcomes (vasopressor, mechanical ventilation and RRT need, daily fluid balance, total dose steroids administered).
L564: - Adverse event evaluation.
L565: Serious adverse events and adverse events graded severe will be collected when these are not outcomes of the study.
L566: Day 5: EQ-5D-5L health questionnaire
L567: Day 28:
L568: One month after inclusion, the patient (or family) will be contacted. In case the patient would be still admitted, a 5th bedside visit will be scheduled. This will allow to determine 28-day mortality.
L569: At the same time the EQ-5D-5L health questionnaire including return to work will be performed (self-complete online or by proxy). The patient will receive a link through e-mail on day 27. There’s a 6 day interval to complete the questionnaire. If the patient hasn’t filled in the questionnaire, he/she will receive a reminding phone call.
L570: Month 3:
L571: The EQ-5D-5L health questionnaire including return to work will be performed for the last time (self-complete online or by proxy). The patient will receive a link through e-mail on day 87. There’s a 6 day interval to complete the questionnaire. If the patient hasn’t filled in the questionnaire, he/she will receive a reminding phone call.
L572: Laboratory tests:
L573: Daily laboratory tests are part of routine clinical care and will be collected (CRP, hematology, chemistry, kidney and liver test). Hematology, kidney and liver testing is necessary to calculate SOFA scores and is standard of care in ED and ICU.
L574: Procalcitonin will be analyzed at d1 and d4. PCT is an effective biomarker for diagnosing sepsis and predicting disease severity and mortality. It’s more specific and sensitive then CRP or leucocytes. This is currently not standard of care in Belgian hospitals. These costs will be borne by the C-EASIE trial.
L575: ABG analysis is part of routine clinical care in ICU. If the patient would be discharged to the ward before day 5, ABG sampling is not considered standard of care, however recommended if clinically indicated (O2Sats below 92%). In order to be able to calculate the SOFA score in this population, we will use the SpO2/FiO2 ratio to impute for PaO2/FiO2 ratio in the respiratory component32.
