L964: | Processes that have been put in place to mitigate risks to participant safety:   Trial-specific adverse event reporting strategy: All SAE’s and severe AE’s will be collected for this trial which will be reviewed by an independent Data Monitoring Committee as defined by the protocol. Medically significant events as defined in the protocol will be captured on a Serious Adverse Event form.    Trial oversight committees (TSC and/or DMC), independent data review A Trial Steering Committee (TSC), Trial Management Group (TMG) and Data Monitoring Committee (DMC) are in place for this phase III trial. The DMC will meet after 50 patients have completed treatment and will review the study data and advise on the continuation of the trial. They will monitor all participating sites until all patients are recruited. The TSC will meet on average 3 times per year the first year and twice a year after that. The DMC will then meet annually to discuss the progress of the trial.    Clinical procedures Daily blood sampling during the day 1-5 are considered as standard care. Daily ABG may cause discomfort and pain to patient of regular sampling. Blood sampling will be performed by skilled staff.  Informed Consent The trial will involve critically ill patients who might be too ill or incapable to give their informed consent. A process of delayed consent, enrolling patients into the clinical trial and obtaining consent as soon as practical from either the patient or their LAR will be applied. | Processes that have been put in place to mitigate risks to participant safety:   Trial-specific adverse event reporting strategy: All SAE’s and severe AE’s will be collected for this trial which will be reviewed by an independent Data Monitoring Committee as defined by the protocol. Medically significant events as defined in the protocol will be captured on a Serious Adverse Event form.    Trial oversight committees (TSC and/or DMC), independent data review A Trial Steering Committee (TSC), T