L966: # Authorisation of participating sites
L967: ## Required documentation
L968: Before the clinical phase of the trial commences all documents as required by GCP should be generated and should be on file. We refer to section 8.2 of the guideline of GCP (https://database.ich.org/sites/default/files/E6_R2_Addendum.pdf).
L969: ## Procedure for initiating/opening a new site
L970: Sites will be authorized to start the study after the initiation visit and when all essential documents as required by GCP and sponsor’s procedures are confirmed and available.
L971: ## Principal Investigator responsibilities
L972: The PI’s legal responsibilities will be listed in the Clinical Study Agreement. Their attendance at the initiation meeting is required. They are responsible for training of new members of the trial team in the protocol and its procedures, ensuring that the ISF is accurately maintained. They will watch over dissemination of important safety or trial related information to all stakeholders within their site as well safety reporting within the timelines.
